This extension adds Shadow of the Tomb Raider modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]TR Mod Manager installed automatically.[/summary]

[b]The extension will automatically download and install the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/shadowofthetombraider/mods/185]SOTTR Mod Manager[/url], which is used to install and enable/disable mods for the game.[/b]
Users may be interested in the[url=https://github.com/Kaldaien/SpecialK/releases/sk_special_projects] custom version of Special K[/url] for installing legacy texture mods. It is no longer auto-installed by the extension and must be installed by the user.
Steam, Epic, GOG, and Xbox versions supported. The Steam Demo is NOT supported.

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]GOG[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Xbox[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]SOTTR Mod Manager installs to the game folder, recognised by a "sottrmodmanager.exe" file.[/*]
[*]TR Reboot Mod Manager installs to the game folder, recognised by a "trreboottools.modmanager.exe" file.[/*]
[*]Binaries / Root Folder mods with a ".dll", ".exe", ".tiger", ".asi" or ".addon64" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Mod Manager mods with a ".tr11dtp", ".tr11material", ".tr11modeldata", ".t11script", ".t11shaderlib", ".tr11sound" or one of 3 other file types install to the "Mods" folder.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Shadow of the Tomb Raider mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Manager:

Recognised when the archive contains a "sottrmodmanager.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Trmodmanager:

Recognised when the archive contains a "trreboottools.modmanager.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Binaries:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".dll", ".exe", ".tiger", ".asi" or ".addon64" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Modmanagermod:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".tr11dtp", ".tr11material", ".tr11modeldata", ".t11script", ".t11shaderlib", ".tr11sound", ".dds", ".tr11objectref", ".tr11dtp" or ".tr11anim" file.

  Installs to: "Mods"

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine.
[/spoiler]

